check 1
# Client state of inv-pick-belt: the 1.14d client unit sets (traces/pc1/client-state/inv-pick-belt.cstate.jsonl, state-snapshot.md section 3 rule 5) against the ClientWorld of d2-client (state-dump --client-out); same save, seed, pokes and input as inv-pick-belt.
# Inventory flow (inv.*): one ground item made by poke `item` (game seed fixed), picked up with
# C->S 0x16, then moved by the sends below; state, packets and items compare both sides.
# Authored by q-run-items. Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md, specs/tools/poke.md, specs/items/inventory-moves.md.
name cs-inv-pick-belt
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 40
seconds 240
channels cstate
at 4 poke seed-game 0x00001234 666
at 4 poke item hp1 @x+1 @y
at 10 send PickItem type=4 id=@4 cursor=0
at 14 send ItemToBelt item=@4 slot=0
